\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces HACOF{} end-to-end flow across the six layers (L1--L6) and six planes. Layers 1--3 (left bracket) carry authority from law to an in-path enforcement point in front of the execution plane. The monitoring plane is out-of-path except where a supervisor's verdict is wired into the gate (Agents A, D, E in Table~\ref {tab:supervisors}; right, inner dashed line). Containment acts back on running workloads (right, outer dashed line). Only human review can send approved policy revisions to the control plane (left, dashed); no automated component edits policy directly. Monitoring and enforcement run continuously across the stack.}}{14}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hacof}{{2}{14}{\hacof {} end-to-end flow across the six layers (L1--L6) and six planes. Layers 1--3 (left bracket) carry authority from law to an in-path enforcement point in front of the execution plane. The monitoring plane is out-of-path except where a supervisor's verdict is wired into the gate (Agents A, D, E in Table~\ref {tab:supervisors}; right, inner dashed line). Containment acts back on running workloads (right, outer dashed line). Only human review can send approved policy revisions to the control plane (left, dashed); no automated component edits policy directly. Monitoring and enforcement run continuously across the stack}{figure.2}{}}
